---
title: Birds
description: Measurement fields for specimens in an Ornithology catalog.
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

Specimens in the `Ornithology` catalog format show the bird measurement form.
Weight units, sex, and life stage work the same way across taxon groups; see
[Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

## Measurements

- `Weight`: specimen weight in the selected unit.
- `Wingspan (mm)`: wingspan length.
- Soft-part colors: `Bill color`, `Maxilla color`, `Mandible color`,
  `Iris color`, `Tarsus color`, and `Toe color`.
- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex controlled vocabulary. Changing
  `Sex` prompts `Change sex?` and clears gonad data that no longer applies.
- `Life stage`: select from the configured life-stage controlled vocabulary.
- `Brood patch`: `Yes` or `No`.
- `Bursa present`: `Yes` or `No`. Choosing `Yes` reveals `Bursa length (mm)` and
  `Bursa width (mm)`.
- `Skull ossification (%)`: `100`, `95`, `90`, `75`, `50`, `25`, `10`, `5`, or
  `0`.
- `Fat`: `None`, `Trace`, `Light`, `Moderate`, `Heavy`, or `Extremely Heavy`.
- `Stomach contents`: notes on stomach contents.

## Gonads

Male gonad fields appear for `Male`, `Male?`, `Gynandromorph`, and
`Hermaphrodite`. Female gonad fields appear for `Female`, `Female?`,
`Gynandromorph`, and `Hermaphrodite`.

| Sex | Field | Options / Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Male | `Left testis size (mm)` — `Size` | `minute` or `1 mm or greater` (reveals `Length` and `Width`) |
| Male | `Remarks` | Notes, such as right testis size |
| Female | `Ovary size` | `Length (mm)` and `Width (mm)` |
| Female | `Appearance` (ovary) | `Smooth`, `Ova minute`, or `At least one ovum ≥ 1 mm dia.` |
| Female | `Diameter of three largest ova (mm)` | `First`, `Second`, `Third`; shown only when ovary `Appearance` is `At least one ovum ≥ 1 mm dia.` |
| Female | `Oviduct` — `Width` | `minute` or `1 mm or greater` (reveals `Width (mm)`) |
| Female | `Oviduct` — `Appearance` | `Straight`, `Convoluted` |
| Female | `Remarks` | Additional gonad notes |

## Molt and notes

- `Molt`:
  - `Body molt`: `None`, `Trace`, `Light`, `Moderate`, or `Heavy`.
  - `Wing molt`: `Yes` or `No`; choosing `Yes` reveals a text field for wing
    molt details.
  - `Tail molt`: `Yes` or `No`; choosing `Yes` reveals a text field for tail
    molt details.
  - `Remarks`: additional molt notes.
- `Notes`: `Habitat` and `Specimen` remark fields.

## Parts and symbionts

Bird catalogs include the `Symbionts` examination fields at the bottom of the
measurement form and the symbiont tab in `Specimen Parts`. See
[Symbionts](/en/usages/specimens/symbionts/).
